.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.vscode/

# Transient command output from device/verify sessions (added 2026-09-25)
# These are captured stdout/stderr of one-off adb, gradle and logcat runs — they belong in the
# session, not in the repo. The helper scripts that produce them (`_core_*.cmd`) ARE tracked.
_build_out.txt
_build_err.txt
_diag_out.txt
_diag_err.txt
_logcat_killwatch.txt
_logcat_killwatch.err
_logcat_killwatch2.txt
_kw2.err
_scroll.err
_scroll2.err
adapter*.txt
android/build-out.txt
android/build-err.txt

# The `_*` convention, decided once (2026-09-28, F7 of V3.3.1_COMPLETION_PLAN.md). The root carries 8
# TRACKED `_*.cmd` / `_*.ps1` helpers -- those are the dev commands and they stay tracked. The 23
# UNTRACKED `_*.txt` files are captures of one-off runs, which is exactly what the twelve named rules
# above already ignore by hand; these two lines finish that sentence instead of naming the next log.
# Nothing dangles: the only `_*` files any doc cites are `_m4_frames.log` and `_m7_regression.log`,
# and `*.log` is ignored above (they are on disk, they are just not version-controlled).
_*.txt
_*.err

